-- WSC/Props/P3Unshaped.lean.disabled — TASK N3: the UNSHAPED P3 attempt against
-- the post-#112 base validator, kept verbatim and re-runnable.
--
-- WHY IT IS `.disabled` (lake ignores the suffix, so this file is NOT part of
-- the `WSC` lean_lib and does not build): every goal in it is measured
-- `⚠️ Undetermined`, and each one costs its Z3 cap in wall time. Left enabled at
-- the caps below it would add ~40 minutes to a library build whose baseline is
-- under 2 minutes, and it would put `⚠️ Undetermined` warnings into a build log
-- whose census is otherwise "N verdicts, 0 errors, all ✅". Neither is worth it
-- for a negative result that does not change.
--
-- WHY IT IS KEPT: the negative result IS the deliverable of `P3_Base.lean`
-- §MEASUREMENT, and a claim of the form "this no longer closes" is only worth
-- as much as the ability to re-run it. Any future improvement to Blaster's
-- handling of `dropList` at a symbolic index — the identified blocker — should
-- be tested by copying the sections below into `WSC/Props/` as `.lean` files and
-- building them.
--
-- HOW TO RE-RUN (from a copy of this repository; do NOT build in a canonical
-- checkout). Split into ONE MODULE PER GOAL: Blaster's `timeout` is per Z3
-- QUERY, not per module (`WSC/Props/P5_NonMember.lean:30` measured that the hard
-- way), so several goals in one module do not each get their own cap and the
-- module can outrun any wall-clock expectation.
--
--   mkdir -p WSC/Probe
--   <split the four sections below into WSC/Probe/{U1,U2,U3,U4}.lean>
--   lake build WSC.Probe.U1 WSC.Probe.U2 WSC.Probe.U3 WSC.Probe.U4
--
-- MEASURED, task N3, wsc-poc main @ 2306678, CLAB @ bbc9f26, PCB @ 9f9ca8c:
--
--   U1  P3, unshaped, budget 600        cap  600 s  ⚠️ Undetermined (602 s)
--   U1  P3, unshaped, budget 600        cap 2400 s  ⚠️ Undetermined (2404 s)
--   U2  negative control, budget 600    cap  600 s  ⚠️ Undetermined (602 s)
--   U3  vacuity probe, budget 600       cap  600 s  ⚠️ Undetermined (602 s)
--   U3  vacuity probe, budget 600       cap 2400 s  ⚠️ Undetermined (2403 s)
--   U4  P3 at the MINIMAL shape (only the redeemer's Data skeleton frozen,
--       everything else symbolic), budget 600      cap 900 s  ⚠️ Undetermined
--   U4  its vacuity probe                          cap 900 s  ⚠️ Undetermined
--   U5  P3, unshaped, budget 250 (K = 194, so 250 still admits the accepting
--       witnesses)                                 cap 900 s  ⚠️ Undetermined
--   U5  its vacuity probe                          cap 900 s  ⚠️ Undetermined
--
-- WHAT THE MEASUREMENT LOCALIZES. U4 freezes the redeemer skeleton and changes
-- nothing (still Undetermined); SHAPES B1RG/B1RS additionally freeze the
-- WITHDRAWAL MAP to two entries and close in under 2 seconds
-- (`WSC/Props/Shaped/P3ShapedR.lean`). So the blocker is the symbolic
-- withdrawal LIST under `pdropList <symbolic index>`, not the redeemer and not
-- the budget. U5 shows a smaller budget does not help either.
--
-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
